tps://api.github.com/repos/joechen0420/lc-off/commits/2e61c64e4d41f300dfa8f5977486f5a39178e2cf", "html_url": "https://github.com/joechen0420/lc-off/commit/2e61c64e4d41f300dfa8f5977486f5a39178e2cf"}], "stats": {"total": 46, "additions": 46, "deletions": 0}, "files": [{"sha": "fe2c458d5c3ab96bc324533c42dee96cd757dc30", "filename": "docs/index.html", "status": "modified", "additions": 46, "deletions": 0, "changes": 46, "blob_url": "https://github.com/joechen0420/lc-off/blob/a8c81bef3ba0ac31ffbdbe826ac6040b1031351e/docs%2Findex.html", "raw_url": "https://github.com/joechen0420/lc-off/raw/a8c81bef3ba0ac31ffbdbe826ac6040b1031351e/docs%2Findex.html", "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/joechen0420/lc-off/contents/docs%2Findex.html?ref=a8c81bef3ba0ac31ffbdbe826ac6040b1031351e", "patch": "@@ -187,6 +187,24 @@\n td.hit{color:var(--moss); font-weight:700}\n td.miss{color:var(--clay); font-weight:700}\n \n+/* Figures keep a light plate in both themes: these are print plots with white\n+   grounds, and inverting them would misrepresent the published artwork. In dark\n+   mode the plate is dimmed slightly so it does not glare. */\n+figure{margin:30px 0}\n+figure .plate{\n+  background:#fff; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:4px;\n+  padding:14px; box-shadow:var(--shadow); overflow-x:auto;\n+}\n+figure img{display:block; width:100%; height:auto; min-width:420px}\n+@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){ figure .plate{filter:brightness(.93) contrast(.97)} }\n+:root[data-theme=\"dark\"] figure .plate{filter:brightness(.93) contrast(.97)}\n+:root[data-theme=\"light\"] figure .plate{filter:none}\n+figcaption{\n+  font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.7; color:var(--ink-3);\n+  margin-top:11px; max-width:74ch;\n+}\n+figcaption b{color:var(--ink-2); font-weight:600}\n+\n .lesson{border-left:3px solid var(--clay); background:var(--clay-soft); padding:20px 24px; margin:28px 0; border-radius:0 4px 4px 0}\n .lesson .tag{font-family:var(--mono); font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--clay); margin:0 0 10px}\n .lesson p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}\n@@ -350,6 +368,14 @@ <h2 data-l=\"en\">One engine, three weight vectors</h2>\n     </div>\n   </div>\n \n+  <div class=\"col\">\n+    <figure>\n+      <div class=\"plate\"><img src=\"figures/figure-01.png\" alt=\"Two-panel figure: the LC-OFF decision path, and the simulated topology\"></div>\n+      <figcaption data-l=\"zh\"><b>\u5716 1</b>\u3000(a) \u5169\u5c64\u6c7a\u7b56\u8def\u5f91\uff1a\u9598\u9580\u628a\u578b\u5225\u5c0d\u61c9\u5230\u6b0a\u91cd\u5411\u91cf\uff0c\u8a55\u5206\u5f15\u64ce\u5728\u4e94\u500b\u6e96\u5247\u4e0a\u6392\u5e8f\u4e09\u500b\u5c64\u7d1a\uff0c\u518d\u7531 DAG \u55ae\u8abf\u6027\u8207\u6bcf\u7bc0\u9ede\u7684\u6536\u5bb9\u8a08\u6578\u5668\u6536\u6582\u7d50\u679c\u3002(b) \u6a21\u64ec\u62d3\u6a38\uff0c\u4ee5\u53ca\u8b93 k*=2 \u6210\u7acb\u7684\u6bcf\u88dd\u7f6e\u9700\u6c42\u8207\u6bcf\u7bc0\u9ede\u7b97\u529b\u3002</figcaption>\n+      <figcaption data-l=\"en\"><b>Figure 1</b>\u3000(a) The two-tier decision path: the gate maps task type to a weight vector, the scoring engine ranks the three tiers on five criteria, and DAG monotonicity plus the per-node admission counter constrain the result. (b) The simulated topology, with the per-device demand and per-node capacity that make k*=2.</figcaption>\n+    </figure>\n+  </div>\n+\n   <div class=\"panel\">\n     <div class=\"panel-head\">\n       <span data-l=\"zh\">\u4e92\u52d5 \u2500\u2500 \u843d\u9ede\u6c7a\u7b56\u5668</span>\n@@ -558,6 +584,12 @@ <h2 data-l=\"en\">A rule is worth something only if it can be wrong</h2>\n       right carries far more than one that never surprises anyone.\n     </p>\n \n+    <figure>\n+      <div class=\"plate\"><img src=\"figures/figure-06.png\" alt=\"Measured optimum against the value the rule names, at three fog capacities\"></div>\n+      <figcaption data-l=\"zh\"><b>\u5716 6</b>\u3000\u4e09\u500b\u9727\u7bc0\u9ede\u7b97\u529b\u4e0b\uff0c\u5be6\u6e2c\u6700\u4f73\u9ede\uff08\u5713\u5708\uff09\u8207\u5f0f\u5b50\u5728\u8dd1\u4e4b\u524d\u6307\u540d\u7684\u503c\uff08\u5716\u4f8b\uff09\u3002\u4e09\u500b\u5168\u4e2d\uff0c\u800c\u4e14\u6bcf\u500b\u6700\u4f73\u9ede\u90fd\u662f<b>\u5167\u90e8\u7684</b>\u2014\u2014\u591a\u6536\u4e00\u53f0\u5c31\u8981\u4ed8\u51fa 1.6 \u5230 2.9 \u500d\u7684\u5ef6\u9072\u3002</figcaption>\n+      <figcaption data-l=\"en\"><b>Figure 6</b>\u3000The measured optimum (ring) against the value the rule commits to before the runs (legend), at three fog capacities. All three agree, and every optimum is <b>interior</b> \u2014 admitting one device beyond k* costs between 1.6\u00d7 and 2.9\u00d7 the latency.</figcaption>\n+    </figure>\n+\n     <h3 data-l=\"zh\">\u63db\u4e00\u7a2e\u62d3\u6a38\u5f62\u72c0\u5462\uff1f</h3>\n     <h3 data-l=\"en\">What about a different topology shape?</h3>\n     <p data-l=\"zh\">\n@@ -824,6 +856,12 @@ <h2 data-l=\"en\">An offline integer, plus one counter</h2>\n       </table>\n     </div>\n \n+    <figure>\n+      <div class=\"plate\"><img src=\"figures/figure-07.png\" alt=\"Fraction of devices meeting a given deadline, all-cloud versus the threshold\"></div>\n+      <figcaption data-l=\"zh\"><b>\u5716 7</b>\u3000\u9054\u6210\u5404\u500b\u622a\u6b62\u6642\u9593\u7684\u88dd\u7f6e\u6bd4\u4f8b\u3002\u5168\u9001\u96f2\u7aef\u662f\u4e00\u9053<b>\u968e\u68af</b>\uff1a215 ms \u4ee5\u4e0b\u6c92\u6709\u4efb\u4f55\u88dd\u7f6e\u9054\u6210\uff0c235 ms \u4ee5\u4e0a\u5168\u90e8\u9054\u6210\u3002\u52a0\u4e86\u9580\u6abb\u4e4b\u5f8c\u66f2\u7dda\u662f<b>\u96d9\u5cf0</b>\u7684\u2014\u2014\u9032\u5165\u9727\u7bc0\u9ede\u7684\u88dd\u7f6e\u65e9\u4e86\u4e00\u500b\u6578\u91cf\u7d1a\u5b8c\u6210\uff0c\u5176\u9918\u5b8c\u5168\u4e0d\u8b8a\uff0c\u6240\u4ee5\u5e73\u53f0\u7684\u9ad8\u5ea6\u6070\u597d\u7b49\u65bc\u88ab\u6536\u5bb9\u7684\u6bd4\u4f8b\u3002</figcaption>\n+      <figcaption data-l=\"en\"><b>Figure 7</b>\u3000Fraction of devices meeting a given deadline. All-cloud is a <b>step</b>: no device meets anything under 215 ms and every device meets 235 ms. Under the threshold the curve is <b>bimodal</b> \u2014 the devices admitted to fog finish an order of magnitude earlier and the rest are unchanged, so the plateau height is exactly the admitted fraction.</figcaption>\n+    </figure>\n+\n     <div data-l=\"zh\">\n       <p>\n         \u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u5217\u503c\u5f97\u505c\u4e00\u4e0b\u3002\u5168\u9001\u96f2\u7aef\u7684\u5ef6\u9072\u5206\u4f48<strong>\u6975\u5ea6\u96c6\u4e2d</strong>\uff1a\n@@ -846,6 +884,10 @@ <h3>\u57f7\u884c\u671f\u8981\u4ed8\u51fa\u4ec0\u9ebc\uff1f</h3>\n         \u4e00\u500b\u96e2\u7dda\u7b97\u51fa\u7684\u6574\u6578\uff0c\u52a0\u4e0a\u6bcf\u7bc0\u9ede\u4e00\u500b\u8a08\u6578\u5668\uff0c\n         \u5c31\u5728\u5ef6\u9072\u8207\u7db2\u8def\u91cf\u5169\u500b\u8ef8\u4e0a\u540c\u6642\u6253\u8d0f\u4e86\u6700\u597d\u7684\u56fa\u5b9a\u7b56\u7565\u3002\n       </blockquote>\n+      <figure>\n+        <div class=\"plate\"><img src=\"figures/figure-05.png\" alt=\"The same configurations on the latency-network plane\"></div>\n+        <figcaption><b>\u5716 5</b>\u3000\u540c\u4e00\u6279\u7d44\u614b\u756b\u5728<b>\u5ef6\u9072\u2013\u7db2\u8def</b>\u5e73\u9762\u4e0a\u3002\u9670\u5f71\u5340\u662f\u300c\u5169\u500b\u8ef8\u90fd\u52dd\u904e\u5168\u96f2\u7aef\u300d\u7684\u5730\u65b9\uff0c\u53ea\u6709 k=1 \u8207 k*=2 \u9032\u5f97\u53bb\uff0c\u800c k* \u5728\u6700\u6df1\u8655\u3002\u60f3\u518d\u964d\u7db2\u8def\u91cf\uff08\u66f4\u5927\u7684 k\uff0c\u76f4\u5230\u5168\u9727\uff09\u5c31\u5f97\u4ed8\u51fa\u5ef6\u9072\u3002</figcaption>\n+      </figure>\n     </div>\n     <div data-l=\"en\">\n       <p>\n@@ -871,6 +913,10 @@ <h3>What does the runtime pay for it?</h3>\n         An integer computed offline, plus one counter per fog node, beats the best fixed\n         policy on latency and network usage simultaneously.\n       </blockquote>\n+      <figure>\n+        <div class=\"plate\"><img src=\"figures/figure-05.png\" alt=\"The same configurations on the latency-network plane\"></div>\n+        <figcaption><b>Figure 5</b>\u3000The same configurations on the <b>latency\u2013network</b> plane. The shaded region is where a configuration beats all-cloud on <b>both</b> axes; only k=1 and k*=2 enter it, and k* sits deepest inside. Lowering network usage further \u2014 larger k, then all-fog \u2014 costs latency.</figcaption>\n+      </figure>\n     </div>\n   </div>\n </section>"}]}